=B => A-1<=k<=B-1. Correct.\n\nadvance_good(L):\n if L<=0 return mask.\n if A==B handle separately outside maybe.\n if L <= 2*B+2 maybe simulate all.\n else:\n   if mask==0:\n      # after L good cells no reachable; but mask remains 0 (all shifts zero)\n      return 0\n   else:\n      # simulate 2B+2 or until full\n      for _ in range(2*B+2):\n         mask=step(mask)\n         if mask==full: break\n      # After 2B+2, should full; but if not? Let's reason. Could be full only when enough. We can simply if mask==full: return full else continue simulate remaining? For safety, we could simulate until full or L done, but L huge. Prove bound maybe 2B. Let's use limit=4*B+10. If still not full with nonzero, maybe due to A=B (handled) or some issue; but A<B should. If not full after limit, we could fall back to simulate up to L but that could be huge; but likely not. Could detect cycle? Not needed. Use while steps<limit and mask!=full. Then if mask==full: return full (since all future good maintain full? if mask full, next newbit=1, shift and mask full remains full, yes).\n      If still not full, maybe simulate L? To be robust for small L? We only enter long L>limit. At this point with A<B, should full. We can return mask? That would be wrong for remaining positions. But we can assert or just simulate all remaining if needed (L up to1e12 dangerous). Let's prove bound from any nonzero mask: choose some reachable p within last B. There exists t<=B-1 such that from p after t steps interval length≥B. The current position when processing cells is c0. p=c0-k. At time s (processing to c0+s), reachable positions from p include p+tA..p+tB for any t<=s (paths of t moves), but also p may be old; however if p is reachable and we process good cells, all positions p+t' for? The interval [p+tA,p+tB] reachable if t steps, independent of intermediate current. At current c0+s with s>=t, those positions are in the past possibly up to p+tB. Need last B positions up to c0+s all within union 